%I A399268 #4 Aug 29 2026 22:26:08
%S A399268 0,0,0,0,0,1,31,592,9019,120668,1486799,17334867,194356753
%N A399268 Number of equivalence classes under rotations and reflections of n-step self-avoiding walks on the 6-dimensional hypercubic lattice that use all six coordinate axes and have no pair of nonconsecutive vertices that are adjacent in the lattice.
%C A399268 In the notation of Nemirovsky et al. (1992), a(n) = p_{n,0}^{(6)}.
%C A399268 Translations are removed by fixing the initial vertex at the origin. The full 46080-element 6-dimensional hypercubic point group of signed coordinate permutations acts on the ordered vertex sequence; path reversal is not included in the equivalence relation.
%C A399268 The values through n=11 follow from the spanning definition, Eq. (7a), and Table II, p. 1094, of Nemirovsky et al. (1992). The values a(12) and a(13) are obtained by inverting Eq. (5) using A038729, A038746, A038748, A323037, and A323063.
%H A399268 A. M. Nemirovsky, K. F. Freed, T. Ishinabe, and J. F. Douglas, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01049010">Marriage of exact enumeration and 1/d expansion methods: lattice model of dilute polymers</a>, J. Statist. Phys., 67 (1992), 1083-1108; see Eq. 5 (p. 1090), Eq. 7a (p. 1093), and Table II (p. 1094).
%F A399268 a(n) = (A038729(n) - 12 - 120*A038746(n) - 960*A038748(n) - 5760*A323037(n) - 23040*A323063(n))/46080 for n >= 1.
%e A399268 a(6) = 1: a representative of the unique equivalence class is the walk whose six steps are in the six distinct positive coordinate directions.
%Y A399268 Cf. A038729 (d=6, m=0 total), A038746 (p_{n,0}^{(2)}), A038748 (p_{n,0}^{(3)}), A323037 (p_{n,0}^{(4)}), A323063 (p_{n,0}^{(5)}).
%K A399268 nonn,walk,more,new
%O A399268 1,7
